/**
 * Day 88 — Phase 5 country pack 5, Southeast Europe: Bulgaria (ROADMAP item 5, second country).
 *
 * Bulgaria had no country timeline. On the globe before the 1815 nations layer, the schematic
 * Byzantine rectangle (keyframes 565, 800, 1025) painted over the whole country from the 6th
 * century to the mid-11th, so the First Bulgarian Empire (681–1018) was invisible, and nothing
 * at all showed the Second Bulgarian Empire (1185–1393) or the Tsardom of Vidin (1356–1396).
 * The Ottoman Balkans ring only reaches Bulgaria from the later 15th century. From 1878 the
 * nations layer draws the Principality of Bulgaria (id `bulgaria`), so this pack uses other ids
 * and has no keyframe after 1396. The Varna necropolis, the Thracians, Roman Moesia and
 * Old Great Bulgaria are timeline items with pins, not outlines.
 *
 * How it is built (docs/DATA.md, "Country-pack globe backfill"):
 *  - 16 new pieces from Natural Earth 1:10m provinces (public domain): Bulgaria's 28 oblasts
 *    grouped into 12 historical regions (Pliska–Preslav, Varna, Silistra–Ruse, Tarnovo,
 *    Lovech–Pleven, Vidin, Sofia, Kyustendil–Blagoevgrad, Plovdiv, Zagore, Burgas, the
 *    Rhodopes), Oltenia, Muntenia and northern Dobruja in Romania, and Greek eastern Macedonia
 *    and Thrace. Clipped to the globe's own land (shapes 128, 124, 132), simplified as one
 *    coverage, and cut back from the Day 87 Serbia pieces, which this pack reuses unchanged
 *    (RS_PIECES) for the Morava lands, Kosovo, North Macedonia, northern Albania, Epirus,
 *    Greek western Macedonia and Thessaly. Generator: et-tools day88-pieces.py (outside the repo).
 *  - A polity is a dated list of pieces; every change is a one-year step. Pieces on different
 *    modern country lands are separate regions, because they do not share vertices there.
 *  - The Byzantine 800 'byzantine-core' rectangle is cut back from the First Empire at each
 *    of its steps (681–1018), using rings precomputed from the same pieces (BYZ_TRIM_RINGS:
 *    the rectangle minus the empire, buffered 0.05°, simplified). The rectangle comes back
 *    whole in 1019 after Basil II's conquest. Byzantine is already off before 1185, and the
 *    Ottoman ring does not reach Bulgaria before 1396, so the Second Empire needs no trim.
 *  - Pieces are regions, not surveyed borders (see each polity's confidence reason).
 */

